IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dog-act-domain`

-- =============================================================================
-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- Part I, Preliminary (remainder)
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of s. 6 ("Application"), s. 7 ("Dogs to be
-- registered") and s. 8 ("Assistance dogs"), as at the compilation dated
-- 28 Nov 2024 [version 08-b0-00], re-verified current 2026-09-09. Source:
-- lines 327-401 of the verbatim compilation
-- (canon/subjects/western-australia/dog-act-1976/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47983.txt).
--
-- Part I -- Preliminary runs ss. 1-8; ss. 1-2 (short title, commencement)
-- and s. 3 (terms used) are outside this file's assigned line range -- s. 3's
-- cross-cutting definitions (LiableParty, DogProfile, "dangerous dog",
-- Penalty) live in dog-act-domain.l4 and are IMPORTed above.
--
-- SCOPED OUT (cited at their site with an @ref comment, never expanded):
-- s. 17 and s. 17(3a) (Part III -- refusal/cancellation of registration,
-- referenced by s. 7(3)(aa)); s. 46(5) (deemed ownership, referenced by
-- s. 6(3)(b)); Prisons Act 1981 s. 3(1) and s. 15A (referenced by
-- s. 6(6)(b)-(c)); Racing and Wagering Western Australia Act 2003 s. 41
-- (referenced by s. 7(3)(d)).
-- =============================================================================

§ `Part I -- Preliminary`
§§ `6. Application`

-- s. 6(1)-(2): the Act applies generally to all dogs (whatever their age or
-- sterilisation status), subject to (4) [Crown dogs, below] and subject to
-- the Highways (Liability for Straying Animals) Act 1983 (an inconsistent
-- provision of that Act prevails). Neither limb has an operative fact of its
-- own beyond the exclusions in (3)/(4) below -- there is nothing else for a
-- downstream rule to test.

DECLARE `S6 Crown Facts` HAS
    -- AMBIGUITY (F-CROWN-PURPOSES): "kept for the purposes of the Crown" is
    -- undefined -- e.g. it is unclear whether a privately-owned dog kept
    -- under a Crown services contract (a contracted quarantine or
    -- explosives-detection dog, say) counts. Taken reading: delegated to
    -- fact-supply, following this corpus's practice for undefined statutory
    -- terms (cf. dog-act-1976.l4's F-REPEATEDLY-TENDENCY, F-ENDANGER-LIFE).
    -- Rejected: attempting a narrower test (e.g. "owned by the Crown") not
    -- supported by the text, which reads "kept for the purposes of", not
    -- "owned by".
    `the dog is kept for the purposes of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 6(1), (4)
GIVEN facts IS A `S6 Crown Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provisions of this Act apply to the dog` facts MEANS
    NOT facts's `the dog is kept for the purposes of the Crown`

-- s. 6(3): notwithstanding the Highways Act carve-out in (2), the owner's
-- (or a s. 46(5) deemed owner's) liability for injury or property damage
-- inflicted by the dog in the course of a highway attack is unaffected.
DECLARE `S6 Highway Liability Facts` HAS
    `party is the owner of the dog`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `party is deemed under s 46(5) to be the owner of the dog`             IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 46(5) -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `injury to a person or animal was inflicted by the dog`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `damage to the clothing or other property of a person was caused by the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury or damage occurred in the course of an attack by the dog on a highway` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 6(2)-(3)
GIVEN facts IS A `S6 Highway Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the party's liability for a highway attack is preserved despite the Highways (Liability for Straying Animals) Act 1983` facts MEANS
        (facts's `party is the owner of the dog` OR facts's `party is deemed under s 46(5) to be the owner of the dog`)
    AND (facts's `injury to a person or animal was inflicted by the dog` OR facts's `damage to the clothing or other property of a person was caused by the dog`)
    AND facts's `the injury or damage occurred in the course of an attack by the dog on a highway`

-- s. 6(5)-(6): a public officer is not guilty of an offence by reason only
-- of taking a dog into a place in the performance of the officer's
-- functions. "public officer" is a checkbox list of independent categories
-- (a)-(e), not a mutually-exclusive enum -- see the "Checkbox
-- relation-on-an-entity" pattern.
DECLARE `Public Officer Facts` HAS
    `is a police officer`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `is a prison officer as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 s 3(1)`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
        -- @ref Prisons Act 1981 s 3(1) -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `is a contract worker as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 s 15A`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
        -- @ref Prisons Act 1981 s 15A -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `is a member of the armed forces of the Commonwealth`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(i)
    `is a member of the Australian Federal Police`                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(ii)
    `is a member of the Australian Quarantine and Inspection Service`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(iii)
    `is a member of the Australian Customs Service`                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(iv)
    `is a person of a prescribed class`                                    IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 6(6)
GIVEN p IS A `Public Officer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a public officer` p MEANS
        p's `is a police officer`
    OR  p's `is a prison officer as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 s 3(1)`
    OR  p's `is a contract worker as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 s 15A`
    OR  p's `is a member of the armed forces of the Commonwealth`
    OR  p's `is a member of the Australian Federal Police`
    OR  p's `is a member of the Australian Quarantine and Inspection Service`
    OR  p's `is a member of the Australian Customs Service`
    OR  p's `is a person of a prescribed class`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 6(5)
GIVEN p IS A `Public Officer Facts`, `dog taken into a place in the performance of the person's functions as a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 6(5) public officer defence is established` p `dog taken into a place in the performance of the person's functions as a public officer` MEANS
        `the person is a public officer` p
    AND `dog taken into a place in the performance of the person's functions as a public officer`

§§ `7. Dogs to be registered`

DECLARE `S7 Registration Facts` HAS
    `dog is registered under this Act or the law of another State or a Territory`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is ordinarily kept or permitted to live in or at premises in Western Australia`              IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `S7 Party` HAS
    `is the owner of the dog`                                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the occupier of the premises where the dog is ordinarily kept or permitted to live`           IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `S7 Exemption Facts` HAS
    `dog is under the age of 3 months`                                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `dog is kept during a period covered by a s 17 application (pending, or until determined, discontinued, or dismissed for want of prosecution) or by a s 17(3a) suspension` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (aa)
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 17, s 17(3a) -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `dog is held in the custody of the Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)
    `dog is held in the custody of the Dogs Refuge Home (W.A.) Inc, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)
    `dog is held in the custody of another prescribed body, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iii)
    `dog is held in the custody of a veterinarian, or a person acting on a veterinarian's behalf, in the course of the veterinarian's professional practice` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)(i)
    `dog is held in the custody of a police officer in the performance of the officer's functions`                          IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)(ii)
    `dog is held in the custody of any other person in the performance of a function under this Act or any other written law` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)(iii)
    `dog is a greyhound registered under the Racing and Wagering Western Australia Act 2003 s 41, while the registration is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
        -- @ref Racing and Wagering Western Australia Act 2003 s 41 -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7(3)
GIVEN exemption IS A `S7 Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dog is exempt from the s 7 registration duty` exemption MEANS
        exemption's `dog is under the age of 3 months`
    OR  exemption's `dog is kept during a period covered by a s 17 application (pending, or until determined, discontinued, or dismissed for want of prosecution) or by a s 17(3a) suspension`
    OR  exemption's `dog is held in the custody of the Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes`
    OR  exemption's `dog is held in the custody of the Dogs Refuge Home (W.A.) Inc, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes`
    OR  exemption's `dog is held in the custody of another prescribed body, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes`
    OR  exemption's `dog is held in the custody of a veterinarian, or a person acting on a veterinarian's behalf, in the course of the veterinarian's professional practice`
    OR  exemption's `dog is held in the custody of a police officer in the performance of the officer's functions`
    OR  exemption's `dog is held in the custody of any other person in the performance of a function under this Act or any other written law`
    OR  exemption's `dog is a greyhound registered under the Racing and Wagering Western Australia Act 2003 s 41, while the registration is in effect`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7(1)(a)-(b)
GIVEN party IS A `S7 Party`, regFacts IS A `S7 Registration Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the party is liable to commit a s 7(1) offence` party regFacts MEANS
        party's `is the owner of the dog`
    OR  (   party's `is the occupier of the premises where the dog is ordinarily kept or permitted to live`
        AND regFacts's `dog is ordinarily kept or permitted to live in or at premises in Western Australia`)

-- The Penalty band turns on whether the dog is a "dangerous dog" (s. 3), the
-- same status distinction as dog-act-1976.l4's F-DANGEROUS-DOG-STATUS-TIMING
-- fork. This file does not re-materialise that fork's Interpretation
-- machinery -- it takes the same reading applied there (status at the time
-- of the offence, i.e. of the alleged non-registration), consistently.
`s 7(1) penalty for an offence relating to a dangerous dog` MEANS
    Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 10_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

`s 7(1) penalty for an offence relating to a dog other than a dangerous dog` MEANS
    Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7(1) Penalty
GIVEN dog IS A DogProfile
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 7(1) penalty` dog MEANS
    IF `the dog is a dangerous dog` dog
    THEN `s 7(1) penalty for an offence relating to a dangerous dog`
    ELSE `s 7(1) penalty for an offence relating to a dog other than a dangerous dog`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7(1)
GIVEN party IS A `S7 Party`, regFacts IS A `S7 Registration Facts`, exemption IS A `S7 Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) offence -- dog not registered` party regFacts exemption MEANS
        NOT regFacts's `dog is registered under this Act or the law of another State or a Territory`
    AND `the party is liable to commit a s 7(1) offence` party regFacts
    AND NOT `the dog is exempt from the s 7 registration duty` exemption

DECLARE `S7 1A Defence Facts` HAS
    `occupier proved that a person over the age of 18, whom the occupier identified, was the owner of the dog at the time of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7(1a)
GIVEN d IS A `S7 1A Defence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 7(1a) defence is established for an occupier` d MEANS
    d's `occupier proved that a person over the age of 18, whom the occupier identified, was the owner of the dog at the time of the contravention`

-- s. 7(2): on a s. 7(1) conviction the court shall, in addition to any
-- penalty, order payment of the unpaid registration fee, recoverable in the
-- same manner as the penalty. Purely a mandatory ancillary consequence of a
-- conviction the court already has before it (no numeric deadline, no
-- further fact for a downstream rule to test) -- recorded here as inert
-- prose rather than a force-fit predicate.

§§ `8. Assistance dogs`

DECLARE `Assistance Dog Facts` HAS
    `trained or being trained by a representative of an organisation prescribed for this definition`         IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `trained or being trained by an individual with the qualifications and experience prescribed for this definition` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `assessed by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) as competent to be an assistance dog`             IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `being assessed by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) to decide whether the dog is competent to be an assistance dog` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `approved, for the purposes of a law of another State or a Territory, as a dog whose use can alleviate or manage an effect of a person's disability or medical condition` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
    `approved by the CEO for the purposes of this definition`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- (f)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 8(1) "assistance dog"
GIVEN dog IS AN `Assistance Dog Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dog is an assistance dog` dog MEANS
        dog's `trained or being trained by a representative of an organisation prescribed for this definition`
    OR  dog's `trained or being trained by an individual with the qualifications and experience prescribed for this definition`
    OR  dog's `assessed by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) as competent to be an assistance dog`
    OR  dog's `being assessed by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) to decide whether the dog is competent to be an assistance dog`
    OR  dog's `approved, for the purposes of a law of another State or a Territory, as a dog whose use can alleviate or manage an effect of a person's disability or medical condition`
    OR  dog's `approved by the CEO for the purposes of this definition`

DECLARE `S8 Entitled Person Facts` HAS
    `has a disability or medical condition an effect of which can be alleviated or managed by the use of an assistance dog` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `is training or assessing an assistance dog and is a representative of an organisation mentioned in the definition of assistance dog paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `is training or assessing an assistance dog and is an individual mentioned in the definition of assistance dog paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `is an individual approved by the CEO as a person to whom s 8(2) applies`                                              IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 8(3)
GIVEN person IS A `S8 Entitled Person Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a person to whom s 8(2) applies` person MEANS
        person's `has a disability or medical condition an effect of which can be alleviated or managed by the use of an assistance dog`
    OR  person's `is training or assessing an assistance dog and is a representative of an organisation mentioned in the definition of assistance dog paragraph (a)`
    OR  person's `is training or assessing an assistance dog and is an individual mentioned in the definition of assistance dog paragraph (b)`
    OR  person's `is an individual approved by the CEO as a person to whom s 8(2) applies`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 8(2)(a)
GIVEN person IS A `S8 Entitled Person Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(2)(a) entitlement to be accompanied by an assistance dog` person MEANS
    `the person is a person to whom s 8(2) applies` person

-- s. 8(2)(b) frames the defence as conditional on the actus reus: the person
-- is "not guilty of an offence BY REASON ONLY THAT he or she takes that dog
-- into or permits that dog to enter" a public building/place or public
-- transport. Mirroring the s 6(5) public-officer-defence pattern above, the
-- act itself is a separate fact parameter, ANDed with s 8(3) membership --
-- not folded away, since without the act there is no offence for the
-- defence to answer.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 8(2)(b)
GIVEN person IS A `S8 Entitled Person Facts`, `person took the dog into, or permitted the dog to enter, a building or place open to or used by the public, or public transport` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(2)(b) defence -- not guilty of an offence for admitting an assistance dog to a public place or public transport` person `person took the dog into, or permitted the dog to enter, a building or place open to or used by the public, or public transport` MEANS
        `the person is a person to whom s 8(2) applies` person
    AND `person took the dog into, or permitted the dog to enter, a building or place open to or used by the public, or public transport`

-- s. 8(4): the CEO may, on application, approve (a) an individual to be a
-- person to whom s. 8(2) applies, or (b) a particular dog to be an
-- assistance dog for the s. 8(1) definition. This is the source of the
-- "approved by the CEO..." facts in the two records above; s. 8(4) itself
-- states a discretionary power with no further operative fact of its own.

DECLARE `S8 Application Facts` HAS
    `made in a manner and form approved by the CEO`                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanied by the prescribed fee, if any, for the application`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanied by each other thing the CEO requires to accompany the application that will enable the CEO to make a decision` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 8(5)
GIVEN app IS A `S8 Application Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 8(4) application satisfies s 8(5)` app MEANS
        app's `made in a manner and form approved by the CEO`
    AND app's `accompanied by the prescribed fee, if any, for the application`
    AND app's `accompanied by each other thing the CEO requires to accompany the application that will enable the CEO to make a decision`

-- s. 8(6): the regulations may provide for review by the State
-- Administrative Tribunal of a CEO decision on a s. 8(4) application.
-- Purely enabling machinery for a body of regulations this Act does not
-- itself state -- no operative fact for a downstream rule to test.
-- s. 8(7): s. 8 applies despite any other provision of this Act or other
-- written law -- a supremacy/override clause, not itself a computed rule.

-- =============================================================================
-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

`a Crown-kept dog` MEANS `S6 Crown Facts` WITH `the dog is kept for the purposes of the Crown` IS TRUE
`an ordinary pet dog` MEANS `S6 Crown Facts` WITH `the dog is kept for the purposes of the Crown` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`the provisions of this Act apply to the dog` `a Crown-kept dog`)
#ASSERT `the provisions of this Act apply to the dog` `an ordinary pet dog`

`a highway attack by the owner's dog` MEANS `S6 Highway Liability Facts` WITH
    `party is the owner of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `party is deemed under s 46(5) to be the owner of the dog` IS FALSE
    , `injury to a person or animal was inflicted by the dog` IS TRUE
    , `damage to the clothing or other property of a person was caused by the dog` IS FALSE
    , `the injury or damage occurred in the course of an attack by the dog on a highway` IS TRUE

`an attack off the highway` MEANS `S6 Highway Liability Facts` WITH
    `party is the owner of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `party is deemed under s 46(5) to be the owner of the dog` IS FALSE
    , `injury to a person or animal was inflicted by the dog` IS TRUE
    , `damage to the clothing or other property of a person was caused by the dog` IS FALSE
    , `the injury or damage occurred in the course of an attack by the dog on a highway` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the party's liability for a highway attack is preserved despite the Highways (Liability for Straying Animals) Act 1983` `a highway attack by the owner's dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`the party's liability for a highway attack is preserved despite the Highways (Liability for Straying Animals) Act 1983` `an attack off the highway`)

`a serving police officer` MEANS `Public Officer Facts` WITH
    `is a police officer` IS TRUE
    , `is a prison officer as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 s 3(1)` IS FALSE
    , `is a contract worker as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 s 15A` IS FALSE
    , `is a member of the armed forces of the Commonwealth` IS FALSE
    , `is a member of the Australian Federal Police` IS FALSE
    , `is a member of the Australian Quarantine and Inspection Service` IS FALSE
    , `is a member of the Australian Customs Service` IS FALSE
    , `is a person of a prescribed class` IS FALSE

`a member of the public` MEANS `Public Officer Facts` WITH
    `is a police officer` IS FALSE
    , `is a prison officer as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 s 3(1)` IS FALSE
    , `is a contract worker as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 s 15A` IS FALSE
    , `is a member of the armed forces of the Commonwealth` IS FALSE
    , `is a member of the Australian Federal Police` IS FALSE
    , `is a member of the Australian Quarantine and Inspection Service` IS FALSE
    , `is a member of the Australian Customs Service` IS FALSE
    , `is a person of a prescribed class` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is a public officer` `a serving police officer`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a public officer` `a member of the public`)
#ASSERT `a s 6(5) public officer defence is established` `a serving police officer` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 6(5) public officer defence is established` `a member of the public` TRUE)

`no s 7 exemption applies` MEANS `S7 Exemption Facts` WITH
    `dog is under the age of 3 months` IS FALSE
    , `dog is kept during a period covered by a s 17 application (pending, or until determined, discontinued, or dismissed for want of prosecution) or by a s 17(3a) suspension` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of the Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of the Dogs Refuge Home (W.A.) Inc, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of another prescribed body, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of a veterinarian, or a person acting on a veterinarian's behalf, in the course of the veterinarian's professional practice` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of a police officer in the performance of the officer's functions` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of any other person in the performance of a function under this Act or any other written law` IS FALSE
    , `dog is a greyhound registered under the Racing and Wagering Western Australia Act 2003 s 41, while the registration is in effect` IS FALSE

`a puppy under 3 months` MEANS `S7 Exemption Facts` WITH
    `dog is under the age of 3 months` IS TRUE
    , `dog is kept during a period covered by a s 17 application (pending, or until determined, discontinued, or dismissed for want of prosecution) or by a s 17(3a) suspension` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of the Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of the Dogs Refuge Home (W.A.) Inc, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of another prescribed body, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of a veterinarian, or a person acting on a veterinarian's behalf, in the course of the veterinarian's professional practice` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of a police officer in the performance of the officer's functions` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of any other person in the performance of a function under this Act or any other written law` IS FALSE
    , `dog is a greyhound registered under the Racing and Wagering Western Australia Act 2003 s 41, while the registration is in effect` IS FALSE

`a dog in RSPCA custody awaiting a new home` MEANS `S7 Exemption Facts` WITH
    `dog is under the age of 3 months` IS FALSE
    , `dog is kept during a period covered by a s 17 application (pending, or until determined, discontinued, or dismissed for want of prosecution) or by a s 17(3a) suspension` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of the Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS TRUE
    , `dog is held in the custody of the Dogs Refuge Home (W.A.) Inc, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of another prescribed body, in a place maintained for finding dogs suitable homes` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of a veterinarian, or a person acting on a veterinarian's behalf, in the course of the veterinarian's professional practice` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of a police officer in the performance of the officer's functions` IS FALSE
    , `dog is held in the custody of any other person in the performance of a function under this Act or any other written law` IS FALSE
    , `dog is a greyhound registered under the Racing and Wagering Western Australia Act 2003 s 41, while the registration is in effect` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`the dog is exempt from the s 7 registration duty` `no s 7 exemption applies`)
#ASSERT `the dog is exempt from the s 7 registration duty` `a puppy under 3 months`
#ASSERT `the dog is exempt from the s 7 registration duty` `a dog in RSPCA custody awaiting a new home`

`the registered dog's owner` MEANS `S7 Party` WITH
    `is the owner of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `is the occupier of the premises where the dog is ordinarily kept or permitted to live` IS FALSE

`an unrelated visitor` MEANS `S7 Party` WITH
    `is the owner of the dog` IS FALSE
    , `is the occupier of the premises where the dog is ordinarily kept or permitted to live` IS FALSE

`kept at WA premises` MEANS `S7 Registration Facts` WITH
    `dog is registered under this Act or the law of another State or a Territory` IS FALSE
    , `dog is ordinarily kept or permitted to live in or at premises in Western Australia` IS TRUE

`the dog is registered` MEANS `S7 Registration Facts` WITH
    `dog is registered under this Act or the law of another State or a Territory` IS TRUE
    , `dog is ordinarily kept or permitted to live in or at premises in Western Australia` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 7(1) offence -- dog not registered` `the registered dog's owner` `kept at WA premises` `no s 7 exemption applies`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(1) offence -- dog not registered` `the registered dog's owner` `the dog is registered` `no s 7 exemption applies`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(1) offence -- dog not registered` `an unrelated visitor` `kept at WA premises` `no s 7 exemption applies`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(1) offence -- dog not registered` `the registered dog's owner` `kept at WA premises` `a puppy under 3 months`)

`a s 7 dangerous dog` MEANS DogProfile WITH
    `declared to be a dangerous dog (declared) under s 33E(1)` IS TRUE
    , `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` IS FALSE
    , `is a commercial security dog` IS FALSE

`a s 7 non-dangerous dog` MEANS DogProfile WITH
    `declared to be a dangerous dog (declared) under s 33E(1)` IS FALSE
    , `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` IS FALSE
    , `is a commercial security dog` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 7(1) penalty` `a s 7 dangerous dog` EQUALS `s 7(1) penalty for an offence relating to a dangerous dog`
#ASSERT `s 7(1) penalty` `a s 7 non-dangerous dog` EQUALS `s 7(1) penalty for an offence relating to a dog other than a dangerous dog`

`an occupier who identified the true owner` MEANS `S7 1A Defence Facts` WITH
    `occupier proved that a person over the age of 18, whom the occupier identified, was the owner of the dog at the time of the contravention` IS TRUE

`an occupier who could not identify an owner` MEANS `S7 1A Defence Facts` WITH
    `occupier proved that a person over the age of 18, whom the occupier identified, was the owner of the dog at the time of the contravention` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `a s 7(1a) defence is established for an occupier` `an occupier who identified the true owner`
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 7(1a) defence is established for an occupier` `an occupier who could not identify an owner`)

`a CEO-approved assistance dog` MEANS `Assistance Dog Facts` WITH
    `trained or being trained by a representative of an organisation prescribed for this definition` IS FALSE
    , `trained or being trained by an individual with the qualifications and experience prescribed for this definition` IS FALSE
    , `assessed by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) as competent to be an assistance dog` IS FALSE
    , `being assessed by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) to decide whether the dog is competent to be an assistance dog` IS FALSE
    , `approved, for the purposes of a law of another State or a Territory, as a dog whose use can alleviate or manage an effect of a person's disability or medical condition` IS FALSE
    , `approved by the CEO for the purposes of this definition` IS TRUE

`an untrained, unassessed, unapproved pet` MEANS `Assistance Dog Facts` WITH
    `trained or being trained by a representative of an organisation prescribed for this definition` IS FALSE
    , `trained or being trained by an individual with the qualifications and experience prescribed for this definition` IS FALSE
    , `assessed by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) as competent to be an assistance dog` IS FALSE
    , `being assessed by a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) to decide whether the dog is competent to be an assistance dog` IS FALSE
    , `approved, for the purposes of a law of another State or a Territory, as a dog whose use can alleviate or manage an effect of a person's disability or medical condition` IS FALSE
    , `approved by the CEO for the purposes of this definition` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the dog is an assistance dog` `a CEO-approved assistance dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`the dog is an assistance dog` `an untrained, unassessed, unapproved pet`)

`a person with a disability alleviated by an assistance dog` MEANS `S8 Entitled Person Facts` WITH
    `has a disability or medical condition an effect of which can be alleviated or managed by the use of an assistance dog` IS TRUE
    , `is training or assessing an assistance dog and is a representative of an organisation mentioned in the definition of assistance dog paragraph (a)` IS FALSE
    , `is training or assessing an assistance dog and is an individual mentioned in the definition of assistance dog paragraph (b)` IS FALSE
    , `is an individual approved by the CEO as a person to whom s 8(2) applies` IS FALSE

`a person with no connection to an assistance dog` MEANS `S8 Entitled Person Facts` WITH
    `has a disability or medical condition an effect of which can be alleviated or managed by the use of an assistance dog` IS FALSE
    , `is training or assessing an assistance dog and is a representative of an organisation mentioned in the definition of assistance dog paragraph (a)` IS FALSE
    , `is training or assessing an assistance dog and is an individual mentioned in the definition of assistance dog paragraph (b)` IS FALSE
    , `is an individual approved by the CEO as a person to whom s 8(2) applies` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is a person to whom s 8(2) applies` `a person with a disability alleviated by an assistance dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a person to whom s 8(2) applies` `a person with no connection to an assistance dog`)
#ASSERT `s 8(2)(a) entitlement to be accompanied by an assistance dog` `a person with a disability alleviated by an assistance dog`
#ASSERT `s 8(2)(b) defence -- not guilty of an offence for admitting an assistance dog to a public place or public transport` `a person with a disability alleviated by an assistance dog` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2)(b) defence -- not guilty of an offence for admitting an assistance dog to a public place or public transport` `a person with no connection to an assistance dog` TRUE)

`a fully compliant s 8(4) application` MEANS `S8 Application Facts` WITH
    `made in a manner and form approved by the CEO` IS TRUE
    , `accompanied by the prescribed fee, if any, for the application` IS TRUE
    , `accompanied by each other thing the CEO requires to accompany the application that will enable the CEO to make a decision` IS TRUE

`an application missing the CEO's required material` MEANS `S8 Application Facts` WITH
    `made in a manner and form approved by the CEO` IS TRUE
    , `accompanied by the prescribed fee, if any, for the application` IS TRUE
    , `accompanied by each other thing the CEO requires to accompany the application that will enable the CEO to make a decision` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the s 8(4) application satisfies s 8(5)` `a fully compliant s 8(4) application`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 8(4) application satisfies s 8(5)` `an application missing the CEO's required material`)
